### Employee Compensation Service: example requests
#
# Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client) and click "Send Request"
# above any request.
#
# Local:  start the API with `npm start`. No key is needed locally.
# Azure:  switch baseUrl to the Azure line below, and add your function key to the .env file
#         (gitignored, never committed):
#           AZURE_FUNCTION_KEY=<key>
#         Get the key with:
#           az functionapp keys list -g rg-compensation-eastasia -n func-compensation-c4p4kq --query functionKeys.default -o tsv

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071/api
# @baseUrl = https://func-compensation-c4p4kq.azurewebsites.net/api
@key = {{$dotenv AZURE_FUNCTION_KEY}}


### Health (no key; also wakes a paused database before a demo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### ─────────────────────────────── Departments

### List departments
GET {{baseUrl}}/departments
x-functions-key: {{key}}


### ─────────────────────────────── Part A: employees

### List all employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### List employees in one department
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?departmentId=2
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### Get one employee (Meera has no bonus: see effectiveBonus and isDefaultBonus)
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees/2
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### Create an employee (only firstName, lastName and salary are required)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
x-functions-key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Riya",
  "lastName": "Joshi",
  "departmentId": 2,
  "salary": 68000.50,
  "hireDate": "2025-01-06"
}

### Give the new employee a bonus (merge patch: other fields stay unchanged)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{created.response.body.employeeId}}
x-functions-key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bonus": 5000 }

### Clear the bonus again (null means "no bonus")
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{created.response.body.employeeId}}
x-functions-key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bonus": null }

### Delete the new employee (204, then 404 if repeated)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{created.response.body.employeeId}}
x-functions-key: {{key}}


### ─────────────────────────────── Error handling

### 400: invalid fields (every problem is listed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
x-functions-key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "", "salary": 100.555, "bonuss": 10 }

### 404: unknown employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees/9999
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### 422: department does not exist
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
x-functions-key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "User", "salary": 50000, "departmentId": 99 }


### ─────────────────────────────── Part B: reports

### 1. Total bonus (no bonus counts as 0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/total-bonus
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### 2. Employees who have never received a bonus
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/employees-without-bonus
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### 3. Bonus as a percentage of salary (2 dp)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/bonus-percentage
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### 4. Departments whose total bonus exceeds their average salary
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/departments-bonus-over-avg-salary
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### 5. Ranking by bonus (no bonus ranked last)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/bonus-ranking
x-functions-key: {{key}}

### 6. Highest salary, and whether that person also has the highest total compensation
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/top-earner
x-functions-key: {{key}}
